33
00:02:45,191 --> 00:02:49,231
And then for
any route update that you receive or

34
00:02:49,231 --> 00:02:52,868
a failure event or configuration change,

35
00:02:52,868 --> 00:02:58,740
you would update the routing table
which is the list of known routes.

36
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:03,683
Perform the locally best route
calculation for that prefix.

37
00:03:03,683 --> 00:03:09,514
And if there's any change to it,
send an update to your neighbors.

38
00:03:09,514 --> 00:03:13,424
So a route here,
when we say the word route,

39
00:03:13,424 --> 00:03:18,285
this is just in the context of BGP,
a path to a prefix and

40
00:03:18,285 --> 00:03:22,727
then a path is a sequence
of autonomous systems and

41
00:03:22,727 --> 00:03:26,357
we'll see an example of this right now.

42
00:03:26,357 --> 00:03:30,353
All right, so in this example,

