67
00:05:27,223 --> 00:05:34,314
So AS3, for example is going to now
going to tell AS2 as well as AS1.

68
00:05:34,314 --> 00:05:40,948
Hey, you can get to D via the path,
AS3, AS4.

69
00:05:40,948 --> 00:05:46,088
So if you want to get to D,
you can go through me, AS3,

70
00:05:46,088 --> 00:05:52,622
then I'll send it to AS4 which told
me that it can reach the prefix.

71
00:05:52,622 --> 00:05:56,149
All right and so
AS2 would have done the same thing,

72
00:05:56,149 --> 00:06:00,409
because it previously received
